      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The explicitly added size validation correctly protects against out-of-bounds reads for version 1 requests, addressing the underlying vulnerability.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The logic fits within the existing Zephyr host command framework by addressing a known limitation of the `SMALLEST_TYPE` validation mechanism, placing the conditional validation properly within the handlers.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** ❌ **Changes Requested** — The explicit validation checks for the base version (v0) in `fp_command_frame` and `fp_command_template` are mathematically redundant and can be deleted. The host command framework already implicitly validates the base size.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Excellent. The logic is placed clearly and uses appropriate internal error codes (`EC_HOST_CMD_REQUEST_TRUNCATED`).\n*   **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** ❌ **Changes Requested** — Automated test coverage is mandatory for all new branch paths and error handling. This CL adds logic to return `EC_HOST_CMD_REQUEST_TRUNCATED` when `input_buf_size` is too small, but there are no unit tests covering these new error paths.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: S (+13, -0). The CL is atomic and focused.\n\n**Missing Test Coverage**\n\nCurrently, the newly added branches returning `EC_HOST_CMD_REQUEST_TRUNCATED` are untested. You must add unit tests to verify these bounds checks, especially since they are security/robustness critical.\n\nFor example, in `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_template.cc`:\n\n```cpp\nZTEST_USER(fpsensor_template, test_fp_template_v1_load_template_truncated)\n{\n\tuint8_t params_buffer[FP_TEMPLATE_V1_PARAMS_BUFFER_SIZE] \u003d {0};\n\tstruct ec_params_fp_template_v1 *params \u003d\n\t\t(struct ec_params_fp_template_v1 *)params_buffer;\n\n\tparams-\u003ecmd \u003d FP_TEMPLATE_LOAD;\n\t\n\t/* Pass a size smaller than required for