      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThe explicit check for the v0 (`struct ec_params_fp_frame`) size is mathematically redundant. The host command framework already guarantees that `args-\u003einput_buf_size` is at least the size of the smallest type via `SMALLEST_TYPE(struct ec_params_fp_frame, struct ec_params_fp_frame_v1)` configured at the bottom of this file.\n\nSince `sizeof(struct ec_params_fp_frame)` **is** the smallest type (8 bytes vs 12 bytes for v1), the framework will drop the command and return `EC_HOST_CMD_REQUEST_TRUNCATED` before it even reaches this handler if the buffer is smaller than 8 bytes.\n\nTo improve code simplicity, remove this redundant check. This will also make the implementation consistent with `fp_command_mode` in `fpsensor_state.cc`, which correctly omits the check for its base version. [🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8434542_c67bb682-bde6-4427-8b4e-19782cc1d189.pb)",
